# Approval Detail Route Reliability

## Canonical route

One detail contract only:

`/app/approvals?request=<approval-uuid>`

- Exact CORE `action_requests.id` UUID required
- Tenant resolved from session — never from URL org params
- No parallel `id`, `approval`, `requestId`, or `actionRequest` query variants without an adapter that normalizes to `request=`

Helpers: `buildApprovalsDeepLink`, `resolveApprovalDetailHref`, `selectFocusedApprovalId` in `lib/companion-action-approval/parse.ts`.

## Navigation

- Executive Command Center, Approval Center list, Kompis, and notifications must emit the same canonical href when an approval ID exists
- Never deep-link a pending card to bare `/app/approvals` as if it were a concrete detail
- Missing/invalid UUID → controlled empty/not-found state — never a crash or generic English global-error page
- Showcase seed cards (`approval_trust`, `ps620:*`, English “Pending Trust Approval” without `request=`) are not actionable pending approvals

## Loader & safety

- Detail loader must not throw for missing, wrong-tenant, expired, cancelled, rejected, or consumed approvals
- Decision buttons require complete valid scope, actionable pending status, and tenant match
- Incomplete scope → disable approve/reject with a clear localized explanation

## Presentation

- Localized error states (`couldNotOpen`, retry, back to approvals, back to Kompis)
- No raw enums, raw ISO timestamps as primary text, or full UUID as primary title
- Status capitalization comes from locale data — no CSS `capitalize` / `uppercase` on status or type labels
- No UnoNight hardcoding in Core

## Forbidden

- Browser/session/MFA handling changes
- Live approval decisions, publish, or rollback in repair tasks
- Dependencies/lockfile changes for this concern
